{"kind":"artifact","text":"The GitHub connector's inbound half at a36ec7fa78abbb1510217b665c8c9eb7f5bac3d7 on request/github-connector-observe. A clause must ask for something nameable — at least one valid issue number, at least one label, or a state it states — and a body that bounds nothing produces no clause rather than an empty criteria clause meaning everything. A malformed issues field is a broken selection rather than a fall-through to criteria, and an unrecognized state is refused here rather than passed to GitHub. Verified against the live workroom under charter b86860f2: the run passes the doorstep, reads only the issue its clause names, and refuses a mismatched owner, a mismatched actor, and the empty charter.","body":{"commit":"a36ec7fa78abbb1510217b665c8c9eb7f5bac3d7","path":"request/github-connector-observe"}}